WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.369 --> 00:00:17.550
I'd lived at Birtwick Park for several years and was happy there.

2
00:00:18.190 --> 00:00:19.591
Even Ginger was content now.

3
00:00:21.592 --> 00:00:23.033
But sad changes were coming.

4
00:00:23.933 --> 00:00:25.974
The mistress was ill more and more often.

5
00:00:26.854 --> 00:00:30.876
The doctor was at the house a lot, and the squire always looked worried and distracted.

6
00:00:32.492 --> 00:00:33.332
"Did you hear the news?"

7
00:00:33.732 --> 00:00:35.713
John asked Little Joe one day in the stable.

8
00:00:37.233 --> 00:00:37.794
"What news?"

9
00:00:38.234 --> 00:00:39.114
Little Joe asked.

10
00:00:40.454 --> 00:00:42.555
"It's the mistress," John said sadly.

11
00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:46.356
"The doctor says her health will only get worse if she stays here.

12
00:00:47.456 --> 00:00:49.817
She needs to move to a warmer place right away.

13
00:00:50.497 --> 00:00:52.078
The whole family will be leaving soon."

14
00:00:53.658 --> 00:00:54.378
"Oh no!"

15
00:00:54.778 --> 00:00:56.239
Little Joe's face went pale.

16
00:00:56.679 --> 00:00:57.619
"Poor mistress.

17
00:00:58.539 --> 00:01:00.600
And what's going to happen to the rest of us?"

18
00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:02.461
"I don't know.

19
00:01:03.542 --> 00:01:04.963
I guess we'll find out soon enough."

20
00:01:07.785 --> 00:01:10.668
After that John was always silent and sad as he worked.

21
00:01:11.709 --> 00:01:13.770
Little Joe hardly ever whistled anymore.

22
00:01:16.493 --> 00:01:21.317
People came and went from the estate more often than usual, and Ginger and I had plenty of

23
00:01:21.417 --> 00:01:22.758
work carrying them around.

24
00:01:23.919 --> 00:01:29.104
The first people to leave Birtwick Park were the squire's young daughters, Miss Jessie and Miss Flora.

25
00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:35.963
The two little girls came to say good-bye to all of us horses, especially Merrylegs, their favorite.

26
00:01:37.284 --> 00:01:40.065
They hugged him so tightly, I thought they'd never let go.

27
00:01:41.386 --> 00:01:44.228
When their nanny pulled them away, both girls were crying.

28
00:01:45.889 --> 00:01:49.230
John and Little Joe looked sadder than ever as they watched the girls leave.

29
00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:53.393
"I suppose that's the beginning of the end," John said.

30
00:01:53.413 --> 00:01:55.694
"Soon the whole family will be gone."

31
00:01:55.714 --> 00:01:59.036
"What will happen to Merrylegs now?"

32
00:01:59.368 --> 00:02:00.268
Little Joe asked.

33
00:02:00.288 --> 00:02:04.130
"The squire says the minister wants him," John replied.

34
00:02:04.150 --> 00:02:09.472
"He needs a pony for his housekeeper to ride on errands, and Merrylegs is perfect for the job.

35
00:02:10.433 --> 00:02:13.794
The minister promised never to sell him, but to keep him for the rest of his life."

36
00:02:15.295 --> 00:02:16.115
"That sounds good."

37
00:02:17.236 --> 00:02:18.856
Little Joe looked at Ginger and me.

38
00:02:18.876 --> 00:02:21.397
"What about the other horses?"

39
00:02:22.618 --> 00:02:27.400
"The squire already agreed to sell Black Beauty and Ginger to an old friend of his," John said.

40
00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:29.360
"They'll have a good home."

41
00:02:30.861 --> 00:02:32.601
I looked at Ginger, and she at me.

42
00:02:33.982 --> 00:02:35.482
This was the first we'd heard about it.

43
00:02:35.962 --> 00:02:37.123
I wasn't sure how to feel.

44
00:02:38.383 --> 00:02:41.564
I'd miss Birtwick Park, but I was glad to have a place to go.

45
00:02:43.084 --> 00:02:46.925
Later we heard that the minister wanted Little Joe to come and work for him and take care

46
00:02:46.965 --> 00:02:47.565
of Merrylegs.

47
00:02:48.986 --> 00:02:49.626
I was glad.

48
00:02:50.066 --> 00:02:52.587
Both of them would be happy to have a familiar face around.

49
00:02:53.727 --> 00:02:56.368
The squire had found new homes for his other horses too.

50
00:02:57.564 --> 00:03:00.246
Soon it was almost time for the squire and his wife to leave.

51
00:03:01.307 --> 00:03:04.390
The squire came to the stable to give us horses a last pat.

52
00:03:06.632 --> 00:03:08.533
"Have you decided what to do with yourself, John?"

53
00:03:08.934 --> 00:03:09.434
he asked.

54
00:03:09.454 --> 00:03:12.857
"I think I want to become a horse trainer," John said.

55
00:03:12.877 --> 00:03:17.541
"I've seen so many horses ruined by bad early training.

56
00:03:18.542 --> 00:03:21.264
I'd love to fix the ruined ones and give others a good start."

57
00:03:21.284 --> 00:03:25.768
"I can't think of anyone better for that kind of job," the squire said.

58
00:03:26.868 --> 00:03:28.529
"I'll write to some friends of mine about you.

59
00:03:28.929 --> 00:03:30.410
I'm sure they can help you get started."

60
00:03:32.251 --> 00:03:36.674
John thanked him, and the squire thanked him in return for his years of faithful service.

61
00:03:37.934 --> 00:03:40.796
For a moment neither man seemed to know what else to say.

62
00:03:41.737 --> 00:03:42.677
Then it was time to go.

63
00:03:43.738 --> 00:03:46.739
The other servants had taken most of the luggage away the day before.

64
00:03:49.001 --> 00:03:52.823
When Ginger and I pulled the carriage to the front door of the house, there were only a

65
00:03:52.883 --> 00:03:54.284
few bags and trunks to load.

66
00:03:55.392 --> 00:03:58.113
Then the squire came out carrying his wife in his arms.

67
00:03:59.234 --> 00:04:02.495
He set her gently inside the carriage, and then climbed in himself.

68
00:04:03.635 --> 00:04:06.216
With a last good-bye to the remaining servants, we were off.

69
00:04:09.118 --> 00:04:11.859
It didn't take long to reach the nearest railroad station.

70
00:04:13.139 --> 00:04:16.501
When we got there, the mistress climbed out of the carriage on her own.

71
00:04:16.521 --> 00:04:21.182
"Good-bye, John," she said in her soft, sweet voice.

72
00:04:21.202 --> 00:04:23.703
"Thank you for everything.

73
00:04:24.104 --> 00:04:24.924
We'll miss you."

74
00:04:30.076 --> 00:04:34.900
Little Joe had climbed out to stand by our heads while the railway workers unloaded the luggage.

75
00:04:36.001 --> 00:04:37.882
I could see tears running down his face.

76
00:04:40.024 --> 00:04:41.905
Soon the train came puffing into the station.

77
00:04:43.106 --> 00:04:47.090
There was lots of hustle and bustle for a few minutes with people getting on and off, and

78
00:04:47.170 --> 00:04:48.130
workers running around.

79
00:04:50.492 --> 00:04:54.716
Then a whistle blew and the train chugged away again, leaving behind nothing but smoke.

80
00:04:56.032 --> 00:04:57.433
John watched the whole time.

81
00:04:58.514 --> 00:05:00.376
When the train disappeared, he sighed.

82
00:05:01.898 --> 00:05:04.320
"We'll never see her again," he said quietly.

83
00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:11.707
"Never." He and Little Joe climbed back onto the carriage, and we set off for home—only it wasn't

84
00:05:11.767 --> 00:05:12.508
our home anymore.

85
00:05:14.269 --> 00:05:17.032
No, Birtwick Park would never be our home again.
